Title: bash-env refuses project .env names that shadow keystore credentials
Created: 2026-09-24
Author: Integration Test

--- log ---
2026-09-24T05:28Z Integration Test created

--- body ---
## Context

Tracker 0942 moved every *harness* credential consumer to point-of-use
resolution, and 0945 removed `KEYS=` and provider loading from `bash-env.sh`.
Nobody audited the downstream projects. A cross-project sweep on 2026-09-24
(57 repos under `~`) found:

- **AEDIST-technical-report**: the project `.env` carries six live
  credentials inline (all copies of `~/.config/keys/` entries). `bash-env.sh`
  still strict-parses the project `.env` and exports every unprotected name,
  so those credentials are resident in every bash subprocess opened there —
  the exact state 0942 set out to end, re-created through the loader's
  surviving half. Filed downstream as AEDIST 0681.
- **climate-finance-het**: `Makefile`, `AGENTS.md`, DMP and
  `pipeline_keystore.py` still document and rely on `KEYS=`; the loader
  now refuses it with a warning on every command. Migration brief handed
  to the Codex session working there.
- **chemin-de-voix**: one script read `MISTRAL_API_KEY` from the environment
  only (fixed, Tracing-Kieu PR #171).

The loader cannot tell a project setting from a smuggled-in credential, so the
fix belongs at the loader, not only in each project.

## Proposal

Extend `_be_is_protected_name` with a dynamic class: any name defined in
`~/.config/keys/*.env` is refused from a project `.env`, with the same
`bash-env: refusing protected name` stderr line (names only, never values).
Parse the keystore for *names* with the same strict KEY= regex; never source
it. Keep the per-subprocess cost bounded (the keystore is ~20 small files;
measure before and after on padme).

Open question for implementation: whether `AGENT_GIT_NAME` /
`AGENT_GIT_EMAIL` (non-secret, but in `github.env`) should stay exportable
from a project `.env`. Default: refuse them too — one rule, no allowlist —
and let the projects that need them resolve at point of use.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A project `.env` defining a keystore name exports nothing for it, and
      stderr names it (test in `tests/test_bash_env_*`, hermetic: fake HOME
      with a fake keystore)
- [ ] `bash -x -c ':'` in such a project exposes no value (xtrace guard still
      covers the new path)
- [ ] Non-keystore names still export unchanged
      (`test_bash_env_project_env_parse.sh` green)
- [ ] Per-subprocess overhead measured on padme, before/after, stated in the
      commit
- [ ] 0942's tracker body gets a note naming the downstream gap and this fix
- [ ] `make check` passes
